    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 06 \u2014 Train & Generate with a Real Character LoRA (optional, fal.ai)\n\nKrea 2 / GPT Image 2.5 / Seedance 2.5 have no LoRA mechanism at all (see README_AI_INFLUENCER.md, 'Where's the LoRA?'). This workflow uses a **different provider**, fal.ai, to actually train one on your canonical reference photos.\n\n**This is a separate account and a separate bill from your Comfy account.**\n1. Get a key at https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys\n2. Put it in `.env` as `FAL_KEY=...`\n3. `pip install -r custom_nodes/ai_influencer_toolkit/requirements.txt` once\n\n## Left: train (run ONCE per character)\nLoad your canonical reference photos (from Workflow 01's output, or your own existing photos \u2014 see README, \"I already have photos\"), batch them, and train. Costs steps x $0.0024 (default 2500 steps \u2248 $6, minimum 1000 steps \u2248 $2.40). Takes several minutes. The resulting LoRA URL is saved into character.json automatically \u2014 you do not need to copy/paste it anywhere.\n\n## Right: generate with the trained LoRA (run anytime after training)\nLoad Character now also outputs `lora_url` straight from character.json. Costs $0.035/megapixel \u2014 e.g. ~$0.03-0.04 per portrait-sized image."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
